            <h2>South America Antarctica Cruise Adventure</h2>

            <p>One of the most unique travel adventures in the world is represented by a South America Antarctica cruise. These cruises usually depart from South America and sail south into Antarctica's icy land. The voyage blends the colorful urban life of South American cities with the pristine wildness of the southern continent. </p>

            <p>As a South America Antarctica cruise traveler, you will be treated to stunning scenery, including glaciers, icy seas and unique wildlife. Cruise lines specializing in expedition travel, like Quark Expeditions and Hurtigruten, are experts at facilitating this type of journey with their guided explorations and education. This kind of cruise combines adventure and discovery in one amazing journey. </p>

            <h2>Cruise Lines that sail in South America</h2>

            <p>Several well-known cruise lines operate voyages throughout South America due to the region's popularity with travelers. Entertainment-cum-scenic travel itineraries are the purview of Royal Caribbean, Carnival Cruise Line and Norwegian Cruise Line. Celebrity Cruises and Princess Cruises offer elegant cruises that emphasize both comfort and destination discovery. </p>

            <p>Luxury cruise lines like the Regent Seven Seas, Silversea Cruises, Seabourn Cruise Line and Ponant Cruises offer a more sophisticated travel experience with custom service and smaller ships. Moving away from port-intensive or “big boat” experiences, Viking Ocean Cruises and Oceania Cruises are ingrained with a cultural exploration and immersive itinerary approach. Each cruise line has its own style, but all let passengers explore South America. </p>

