            <p>That is why passengers on a cruise to South America have the chance of visiting all sorts of landscapes, as well as a great variety of cultures. Historic architecture, local markets and lively music are found in coastal cities. Visitors can stroll through colonial neighborhoods, wander into museums or savour local fare in waterside restaurants. </p>

            <p>Natural attractions are equally impressive. The continent features dramatic fjords in Chile, tropical forests and stunning coastal scenery. And the wildlife and landscapes that you see at each port of call are unforgettable. This diversity is precisely one of the reasons a cruise to South America remains attractive to travelers from all over the world. </p>

